From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:23:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: drop the secure UI platform pieces

libsecureuisvc_jni.so (system_ext) links libgui by the pre-Android-17
SurfaceComposerClient::createSurface signature and no longer resolves:

  FAILED: .../libsecureuisvc_jni.so.check_elf_file
  error: Unresolved symbol: _ZN7android21SurfaceComposerClient13createSurfaceE...

It is the JNI half of com.qualcomm.qti.services.secureui, the trusted-UI
PIN pad the stock ROM used for payment apps; nothing in Lineage talks to
it. Drop the app and the three system_ext libraries that exist only for
it (libsecureuisvc_jni, libsecureui_svcsock_system and the system_ext
copy of vendor.qti.hardware.tui_comm@1.0). The vendor side (libsecureui,
libsecureui_svcsock, tui_comm@1.0_vendor and its service) stays; the
HIDL service is still declared in manifest.xml and the framework matrix.

Of the 14 system/system_ext/product blob libraries in this tree, this is
the only one with an unresolved symbol against the lineage-24.0 staging.
---
 Android.bp       | 103 -----------------------------------------------
 bonito-vendor.mk |   4 --
 2 files changed, 107 deletions(-)

